<title>USA: US tube makers cite concern over Malaysian imports.</title>
<headline>US tube makers cite concern over Malaysian imports.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of manufacturers producing stainless steel pipes and tubes on Thursday said the producers would be monitoring imports of the tubing from Malaysia after a recent jump in the volume of such imports.</p>
<p>According to the Specialty Tubing Group, a coalition of U.S. pipe and tube producers, imports of welded stainless steel pipe and tube from Malaysia in the first 10 months of 1996 totaled 2,656 tons, a 139 percent increase from the same period last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Our ongoing monitoring of imports indicates a rapid acceleration of welded stainless steel pipe coming from Malaysia at strikingly depressed prices,&quot; the coalition said in a statement, adding it would seek redress if necessary.</p>
</text>
